+## 2.17 Post-17 July implementation delta
+
+The following current public retrieval hierarchy supersedes polling/pane-capture
+wording elsewhere in older bridge prose:
+
+```text
+exact coordination message
+→ xtmux message-get <message-key> --json
+
+latest completed generic interactive turn
+→ xtmux agent-last <pane|session> --json
+
+structured Specialist progress
+→ sp run --json / sp feed --json
+
+authoritative complete Specialist result
+→ sp result <job-id> --json
+
+live prompt/menu/auth/streaming diagnosis
+→ bounded pane capture
+```
+
+Pane capture is not a result protocol. `sp feed --json` is a structured progress
+surface, not the terminal-result authority.
+
+Additional current-state consequences:
+
+- `sp render-bead` is the landed Specialists-owned roleless turn-1 renderer. Any
+  remaining Core consumption/assignment work must reuse it rather than create a
+  second Bead traversal or mandatory-rule renderer.
+- `xtrm.branch.integration.v1` has public write and read surfaces. Remaining work is
+  correctness of attribution/targets and consumption, not invention of a new merge
+  state store.
+- Core topology already supplies a read-only cross-system projection and operator
+  views. Console/roadmap work consumes or supersedes that contract explicitly rather
+  than recreating an independent mutable topology graph.
+- The current NDJSON projector provides a thin workflow-adapter boundary:
+
+  ```text
+  start sp run --json
+  → consume ordered public events
+  → observe terminal settlement
+  → retrieve sp result --json
+  ```
+
+  Archon remains experimental and may consume this boundary; it does not own
+  Specialists lifecycle, Beads, xtmux, worktrees or Git integration truth.
+
